{"book": "gate-da", "num": 60, "label": "60", "slug": "60-ml-unsupervised-dimensionality-reduction", "title": "Dimensionality Reduction", "tag": "Machine Learning: Unsupervised", "summary": "Dimensionality reduction is crucial in machine learning when dealing with high-dimensional datasets. High dimensions lead to several challenges:", "wordCount": 412, "readingTimeMin": 2, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "60.1", "title": "Principal Component Analysis (PCA)", "blocks": [{"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Introduction and Motivation", "id": "introduction-and-motivation"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Dimensionality reduction is crucial in machine learning when dealing with high-dimensional datasets. High dimensions lead to several challenges:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Curse of dimensionality:</b> Distances become less meaningful as dimensionality increases."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Visualization:</b> Difficult to visualize data beyond 3 dimensions."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Computational cost:</b> More features mean more computation in ML models."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Redundancy:</b> Many features are correlated and carry overlapping information."}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "PCA Concept", "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Idea:</b> PCA transforms the original correlated features into a smaller set of uncorrelated variables called <b>principal components (PCs)</b> while retaining most of the variance in the data."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Benefits:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Reduces dimensionality and computational cost."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Removes feature correlations."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Preserves maximum variance."}]}]}]}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Visualization of PCA Projection", "id": "visualization-of-pca-projection"}, {"t": "fig", "num": null, "figs": [], "srcs": ["/books/gate-da/mlu/fig014.png"], "caption": ""}, {"t": "h", "level": 3, "x": "Mathematical Formulation", "id": "mathematical-formulation"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Setup Assuming population data:</b>\n\nLet there be $n$ data points and $d$ features."}, {"t": "math", "x": "X =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\nx_{11} & x_{12} & \\cdots & x_{1d} \\\\\nx_{21} & x_{22} & \\cdots & x_{2d} \\\\\n\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\nx_{n1} & x_{n2} & \\cdots & x_{nd}\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times d}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Here,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "i = 1,\\dots,n \\quad (\\text{samples}), \\qquad\nj = 1,\\dots,d \\quad (\\text{features})"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Data Standardization (Zero Mean, Unit Variance)</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Mean of feature $j$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_j = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_{ij}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Standard deviation of feature $j$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_j = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^{n} (x_{ij} - \\mu_j)^2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Standardized data:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "z_{ij} = \\frac{x_{ij} - \\mu_j}{\\sigma_j}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Standardized Data Matrix</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Z =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\nz_{11} & z_{12} & \\cdots & z_{1d} \\\\\nz_{21} & z_{22} & \\cdots & z_{2d} \\\\\n\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\\nz_{n1} & z_{n2} & \\cdots & z_{nd}\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times d}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Covariance Matrix</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C = \\frac{1}{n} Z^{T} Z\n\\quad \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times d}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Properties:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C = C^T \\quad (\\text{symmetric})"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lambda_i \\ge 0 \\quad (\\text{positive semi-definite})"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 4: Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Solve:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "|C - \\lambda I| = 0"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C v_i = \\lambda_i v_i"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Eigenvalues ordered as:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lambda_1 \\ge \\lambda_2 \\ge \\cdots \\ge \\lambda_d \\ge 0"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Interpretation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lambda_i \\rightarrow \\text{variance along direction } v_i"}, {"t": "math", "x": "v_i \\rightarrow \\text{principal axis}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 5: Selection of Principal Components</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Choose top $k$ eigenvectors corresponding to largest eigenvalues."}, {"t": "math", "x": "W = [v_1 \\; v_2 \\; \\cdots \\; v_k] \\in \\mathbb{R}^{d \\times k}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Explained variance ratio:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\text{Variance explained by } \\lambda_i\n=\n\\frac{\\lambda_i}{\\sum_{j=1}^{d} \\lambda_j}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 6: Projection (Dimensionality Reduction)</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Y = Z W"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Y \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times k}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "This gives the representation of data in the new principal component space."}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": "Key Notes", "blocks": [{"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Principal components are orthogonal."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "First PC captures maximum variance."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Total variance in data = sum of eigenvalues."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Fraction of variance captured by $i$-th PC: $\\lambda_i / \\sum_j \\lambda_j$"}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "9", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Given Data</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "X =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n2 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 1 \\\\\n3 & 1 \\\\\n4 & 3\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{4 \\times 2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Here, $n = 4$ samples and $d = 2$ features."}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Compute Mean and Standard Deviation</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Mean of each feature:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu_1 = \\frac{2+0+3+4}{4} = 2.25,\n\\quad\n\\mu_2 = \\frac{0+1+1+3}{4} = 1.25"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Standard deviation:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_1 = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}\\left[(2-2.25)^2 + (0-2.25)^2 + (3-2.25)^2 + (4-2.25)^2\\right]} = 1.479"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\sigma_2 = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}\\left[(0-1.25)^2 + (1-1.25)^2 + (1-1.25)^2 + (3-1.25)^2\\right]} = 1.090"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Standardization</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "z_{ij} = \\frac{x_{ij} - \\mu_j}{\\sigma_j}"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Z =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n-0.17 & -1.15 \\\\\n-1.52 & -0.23 \\\\\n0.51 & -0.23 \\\\\n1.18 & 1.61\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{4 \\times 2}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Covariance Matrix</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C = \\frac{1}{n} Z^T Z"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n1.00 & 0.69 \\\\\n0.69 & 1.00\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 4: Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "|C - \\lambda I| = 0"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lambda_1 = 1.69, \\quad \\lambda_2 = 0.31"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Corresponding eigenvectors:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "v_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n1 \\\\ 1\n\\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad\nv_2 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n1 \\\\ -1\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 5: Selection of Principal Component</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2} = \\frac{1.69}{2} = 84.5\\%"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Select $k = 1$ principal component."}, {"t": "math", "x": "W = v_1 =\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n1 \\\\ 1\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 6: Projection</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Y = Z W"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Y =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n-0.93 \\\\\n-1.23 \\\\\n0.20 \\\\\n1.96\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{4 \\times 1}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Final Result</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "The original 2D data is reduced to 1D while preserving maximum variance."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "10", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Given Data</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "X =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n2 & 2 & 3 \\\\\n3 & 3 & 4 \\\\\n4 & 4 & 5 \\\\\n5 & 5 & 6\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\in \\mathbb{R}^{4 \\times 3}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "The three features $X_1, X_2, X_3$ are highly correlated."}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 1: Standardization (Mean Centering)</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Compute the mean of each feature:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\mu =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n3.5 & 3.5 & 4.5\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Centered data matrix:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Z = X - \\mu =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n-1.5 & -1.5 & -1.5 \\\\\n-0.5 & -0.5 & -0.5 \\\\\n0.5 & 0.5 & 0.5 \\\\\n1.5 & 1.5 & 1.5\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 2: Covariance Matrix</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C = \\frac{1}{n} Z^T Z"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since all features move together, the covariance matrix has large off-diagonal entries:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n\\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2 \\\\\n\\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2 \\\\\n\\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2 & \\sigma^2\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "This indicates strong positive correlation among $X_1, X_2, X_3$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Step 3: Eigenvalue Decomposition</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Solve:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "C v = \\lambda v"}, {"t": "p", "x": "The dominant eigenvector is:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "v_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "This direction captures maximum variance."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Remaining eigenvectors are orthogonal to $v_1$ and correspond to very small eigenvalues, capturing negligible variance."}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Interpretation</b>"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\lambda_1 \\gg \\lambda_2, \\lambda_3"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Most of the variance lies along the direction $(1,1,1)$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Therefore, the original 3D data can be projected onto a single principal component:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Y = Z v_1"}, {"t": "p", "x": "This reduces the data from $\\mathbb{R}^3$ to $\\mathbb{R}^1$ while preserving most of the information."}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Conclusion</b>"}, {"t": "p", "x": "PCA effectively reduces the dimensionality from 3 to 1 due to high correlation among features."}]}]}], "sectionCount": 1}